  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESTART III &#x2013; Support for the Austrian Return System and the Reintegration of Voluntary Returnees in Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to contribute to quality return counselling by making sure that return counsellors have access to quality management tools, such as assisted voluntary returns and reintegration (AVRR) guidelines and targeted trainings on processes and standards in the field of AVRR according to IOM policies and guidelines. In addition, the project aims at strengthening the exchange and cooperation between all stakeholders involved in the area of AVRR and will ensure that professionals involved in the provision of assistance to voluntary returnees, including to migrants in vulnerable situations, will have access to information and possibilities for exchange. In addition, the project aims to raise awareness among persons interested in voluntarily returning from Austria to Afghanistan and to provide 400 beneficiaries with all necessary support measures in order to guarantee their safe, timely and dignified voluntary return to Afghanistan. The project will address the most urgent needs of these project beneficiaries immediately after their return, provide assistance to their socio-economic reintegration, and support them in situations of vulnerability in covering their individual needs.</narrative>
  </description>
